From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:19:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] replay: declare replay_mutex_locked() in system/replay.h

0028 calls replay_mutex_locked() from system/cpus.c, but it was declared
only in replay/replay-internal.h, which cpus.c does not include. gcc 13
treats the implicit declaration as a warning (and --disable-werror hides
it); clang and gcc 14 reject it, so the series did not build on macOS.

Move the declaration next to replay_mutex_lock()/unlock().
---
 include/system/replay.h  | 1 +
 replay/replay-internal.h | 1 -
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/system/replay.h b/include/system/replay.h
index 3b00386821b6b99c8f4d88a85ffc36d8ffd773f7..59314d26ae3a7bde1a69c7aa3b55f2e09801e62d 100644
--- a/include/system/replay.h
+++ b/include/system/replay.h
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ extern char *replay_snapshot;
 
 void replay_mutex_lock(void);
 void replay_mutex_unlock(void);
+bool replay_mutex_locked(void);
 
 /* Processing the instructions */
 
diff --git a/replay/replay-internal.h b/replay/replay-internal.h
index 42c393542eb3151564c62a7383788502782d4b2f..2f8df0b3ff4c070ab302cce1182d22c292732e29 100644
--- a/replay/replay-internal.h
+++ b/replay/replay-internal.h
@@ -126,7 +126,6 @@ void replay_get_array_alloc(uint8_t **buf, size_t *size);
  * synchronisation between vCPU and main-loop threads. */
 
 void replay_mutex_init(void);
-bool replay_mutex_locked(void);
 
 /*! Checks error status of the file. */
 void replay_check_error(void);
